title: Payers › Workflow Builder › Version history and restore
route: /payers/summit?tab=builder
intro: Every saved draft, publish and archive is kept as a version with who made it, when, and why. A version can be read on a read-only canvas and restored as a new draft. Restoring never overwrites anything: the published version stays in force until a person publishes the draft.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Click 'More', then 'Version history'"
overlay o1 "Right-hand panel 'Version history'\n'Retroactive Authorization. Every save and publish is kept, with who and why.'\nNewest first"
screen v1 "One row per version\nv2 in a circle, a pill Draft, Published or Archived, 'Latest saved' on the newest,\nthe reason, 'Jordan Perez · Tue 10:42 am · 22 steps'"
decision d0 "Any version saved yet?"
screen e0 "'No version has been saved yet.'"
click c1 "Click 'Preview' on a row"
screen pv "Read-only canvas of that version under the row\nRequest type and dates, 'Read only.'\nPan and zoom work, nothing can be changed"
click c2 "Click 'Hide preview'"
click c3 "Click 'Restore as a draft' on a row"
screen rs "Under the row\n'Restoring makes version N's steps the new draft. The published version stays in force until a person publishes the draft.'\n'Cancel' and 'Restore as a new draft'"
click c4 "Click 'Restore as a new draft'"
store st1 "A new draft is made from that version's steps and settings\nOne version number higher than anything saved before\nEdit log entry and a version line 'Restored version N'"
toast t1 "'Restored as a draft'\n'... version N is now draft version M. The published version has not changed.'"
process p1 "The panel closes and the new draft opens on the canvas"
click c5 "Click 'Cancel', X, or press Escape"
process p2 "Panel closes, nothing changes"
end e1 "The earlier version is a draft again, ready to edit and publish"
goto g1 "Continues in: Payers › History & Changes › Read what changed"

s1 --> o1 --> d0
d0 -->|No| e0
d0 -->|Yes| v1
v1 --> c1 --> pv --> c2 --> v1
v1 --> c3 --> rs --> c4 --> st1 --> t1 --> p1 --> e1
rs --> c5 --> p2
o1 --> c5
e1 --> g1
